<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Sondershausen</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Sondershausen is a town in northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/thuringia">Thuringia</a>, below the Hainleite hills. It was the residence of the counts, later princes, of Schwarzburg-Sondershausen from 1599 until 1918, and their palace keeps rooms from the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/renaissance">Renaissance</a> to neoclassical periods. The town has a long musical tradition based on the princely court orchestra, and its old potash mine is now open to visitors.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/sondershausen.jpg" alt="Sondershausen" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Karl-Heinz Herrmann · CC BY-SA 2.0 de · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Stadtzentrum-Sondershausen.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
